## Why This Is Asked
Tests on-device multilingual NLP, lightweight features, data labeling, evaluation, and privacy-conscious deployment.

## Key Concepts
- On-device inference with strict size limits
- Multilingual handling via shared vocab + language token
- Lightweight features: bag-of-words + character n-grams
- Evaluation: macro-F1 by language; latency targets; privacy by local processing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal feature extractor and predictor sketch (pseudo)
function featurize(text, vocab){
  const tokens = text.toLowerCase().split(/\W+/);
  const vec = new Array(vocab.length).fill(0);
  tokens.forEach(t => { const idx = vocab.indexOf(t); if (idx>=0) vec[idx]+=1; });
  return vec;
}
function predict(vec, weights){
  let score=0; for(let i=0;i<vec.length;i++) score += vec[i]*weights[i];
  return score>0 ? 1 : 0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle class imbalance across labels?
- What offline evaluation metrics beyond macro-F1 would you consider for drift?

## Why This Is Asked

Covers on-device NLP, privacy, multilingual support, and practical rollout in fintech contexts. Introduces regulatory-signal detection as a distinct angle from prior questions.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference vs. cloud; model size planning; rule-based vs. lightweight ML
- Multilingual handling (EN/FR/JA) and term coverage across scripts
- Explainability and confidence calibration for risk flags
- Privacy controls and compliant data labeling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Tiny heuristic-based detector skeleton (pseudo)
class RegRiskDetector {
  constructor(vocab) { this.vocab = vocab; }
  score(text) { return this.vocab.some(t => text.includes(t)) ? 0.9 : 0.1; }
  explain(text) { return this.score(text) > 0.5 ? 'Flag due to regulatory term' : 'No risk'; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate false positives in offline tests?
- What strategies for multilingual term expansion and drift handling would you employ?
